backport: fix the content box and zero font size for single-line fields (bug 709471)

BACKPORT of upstream mupdf 38958bd665b6e57fa19e1024871dc196fc36da49, not a
change of ours. Drop it when the vendored mupdf moves past that commit - it is
on mupdf master but not in 1.28.2, which comes off a maintenance branch that
forked at 205b8cf43, before it.

https://bugs.ghostscript.com/show_bug.cgi?id=709471

Two fixes to the rich-text appearance path:
  - the content box for a single-line field was computed wrongly, putting the
    text entirely outside the clipped area, i.e. rendering it blank
  - a /DA font size of 0 stayed 0, so a FreeText annotation rendered at
    font-size:0. It now defaults to 12pt (and to the field height for a
    single-line widget).

This overlaps with 0009 but does not replace it. On its own it makes issue
#5404 render, but as two wrapped lines in a single-line field, because
upstream's auto-size for that case is the field height and the width is not
measured (their own TODO). 0009 keeps CP-1250 text on the simple path, whose
auto-size does fit the width, so with both applied #5404 renders on one line
exactly as it does today. Nor is this the more general fix it looks like:
pdf_add_substitute_font() is still a stub upstream, so text needing a font we
cannot embed (Turkish, Vietnamese, ...) renders blank on the rich path either
way.

What it buys us today is the FreeText size-0 case, which 0009 does not touch.
---
diff --git a/source/pdf/pdf-appearance.c b/source/pdf/pdf-appearance.c
index 6395623..ab82fa3 100644
--- a/source/pdf/pdf-appearance.c
+++ b/source/pdf/pdf-appearance.c
@@ -2304,9 +2304,8 @@ write_rich_content(fz_context *ctx, pdf_annot *annot, fz_buffer *buf, pdf_obj **
 	// this matches the math in write_variable_text.
 	if (!multiline)
 	{
-		float ty = ((h - b * 2) - size) / 2;
-		content_box.y0 = h - b - 0.8f * size + ty;
-		content_box.y1 = content_box.y0 + size * 2;
+		float gap = (h - b*2 - size) / 2;
+		content_box = fz_make_rect(b, b + gap, w - b * 2, h + gap + size * 2);
 	}
 
 	fz_try(ctx)
@@ -2577,6 +2576,10 @@ pdf_write_free_text_appearance(fz_context *ctx, pdf_annot *annot, fz_buffer *buf
 	lang = pdf_annot_language(ctx, annot);
 	rd = pdf_annot_rect_diff(ctx, annot);
 
+	/* FreeText is always multi-line so default size to 12pts if it is zero. */
+	if (size <= 0)
+		size = 12;
+
 	/* /Rotate is an undocumented annotation property supported by Adobe.
 	 * When Rotate is used, neither the box, nor the arrow move at all.
 	 * Only the position of the text moves within the box. Thus we don't
@@ -2764,6 +2767,9 @@ pdf_write_tx_widget_appearance(fz_context *ctx, pdf_annot *annot, fz_buffer *buf
 		rc = free_rc = escape_text(ctx, text);
 		if (!ds)
 		{
+			// TODO: measure accurate width to fit box if single-line!
+			if (size <= 0)
+				size = (ff & PDF_TX_FIELD_IS_MULTILINE) ? 12 : h - b*2;
 			fz_snprintf(ds_buf, sizeof ds_buf,
 				"font-family:%s;font-size:%gpt;color:#%06x;text-align:%s",
 				full_font_name(&font),
